From 631893bdf40ab2cb7a8bc9a25216982e60e76211 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Karlsson <daniel.karlsson9@inter.ikea.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Dec 2025 11:18:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Align host name TTL with default TTL

The host name TTL was previously set to 120 seconds while all other
records used 75 minutes. This inconsistency caused host records to expire
much earlier than associated service records, resulting in frequent
re-registrations that violated Apple HomeKit certification chattiness tests.

This commit increases AVAHI_DEFAULT_TTL_HOST_NAME from 120 seconds to
75 minutes (4500 seconds) to match AVAHI_DEFAULT_TTL. The host name TTL
is now defined in terms of the default TTL to eliminate duplication and
ensure both values remain synchronized.

With this change, host records and service records have consistent
lifetimes, reducing mDNS traffic to meet HomeKit certification requirements.

CAVEAT: The increased TTL may cause stale host information in dynamic
network environments:
- Devices that change IP addresses will have stale entries cached for up
  to 75 minutes, potentially causing connection failures
- Devices that leave the network ungracefully (power loss, crash) will
  appear reachable for up to 75 minutes
- Network topology changes will be less responsive

This change is appropriate for stable deployments where devices maintain
consistent IP addresses and rarely disconnect, such as typical Apple
HomeKit installations. For more dynamic environments, consider alternative
TTL values.
---
 avahi-common/defs.h | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/avahi-common/defs.h b/avahi-common/defs.h
index bb73a9d..9d00b19 100644
--- a/avahi-common/defs.h
+++ b/avahi-common/defs.h
@@ -345,12 +345,12 @@ enum {
 
 /** @} */
 
-/** The default TTL for RRs which contain a host name of some kind. */
-#define AVAHI_DEFAULT_TTL_HOST_NAME (120)
-
-/** The default TTL for all other records. */
+/** The default TTL for all records. */
 #define AVAHI_DEFAULT_TTL (75*60)
 
+/** The default TTL for RRs which contain a host name of some kind. */
+#define AVAHI_DEFAULT_TTL_HOST_NAME AVAHI_DEFAULT_TTL
+
 AVAHI_C_DECL_END
 
 #endif
